Description: CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 for PHP 5.6: the official EOL fix "Avoid state corruption via bailout" (PHP 7.4) carried over to the PHP 5 engine, as proposed for remicollet/php-src-security in pull request #32: fatal errors of the allocator (memory limit, integer overflow in allocation sizes, string size overflow in concatenation, Balloc) print and _exit() the worker instead of a zend_error() longjmp() out of a half-initialized request; state that an error before the next request startup can reach is reset (user error and exception handler stacks, error handling mode, exception, the autoload guard table, freed $_GET/$_POST/... pointers, SAPI request strings, modules_activated, zend_llist head and tail); multipart parsing keeps only Content-Disposition and Content-Type headers, without duplicates; session upload progress stays off whatever session.upload_progress.enabled says. The code of that pull request as it is, so that sync skips this patch once the branch has it; what the official fix and the other 5.6 ports have on top is in backport-php2shell-2-extra.patch.
Origin: https://github.com/remicollet/php-src-security/pull/32 (RalphJS, 22.10.2026), commit 477c04a64, port of php-src 802c21075308 (PHP 7.4, Arnaud Le Blanc) to PHP-5.6-security-backports-openssl11 @ 5c2cc46b45cf; the same code as our own port of 22.10.2026 (131fde85f), which it replaces. Skipped by sync once the branch has it

